# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Agent application form — where submitted applications are delivered.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Set this to any URL that accepts a JSON POST and the form will send
# applications straight there. Works with Formspree, Getform, Basin, a
# Google Apps Script web app, or your own API route.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_AGENT_FORM_ENDPOINT=https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxxx
#
# Leave it unset and the form still works: it hands the completed
# application to WhatsApp (or email) as a pre-filled message, using the
# numbers configured in src/lib/site.ts.
#
# Note the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — this value is visible in the browser, so
# use an endpoint designed to receive public form posts, never a secret key.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_AGENT_FORM_ENDPOINT=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Customer reviews — where reviews submitted on /customer-feedback go.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Same arrangement as the agent form above: any URL that accepts a JSON POST.
# Leave it unset and the form hands the review to WhatsApp as a pre-filled
# message instead.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_REVIEW_FORM_ENDPOINT=
